<p>We invite faculty, students, industry partners, and academic leaders to engage with
emerging scholars whose work represents the future of artificial intelligence and
computing innovation at the 2nd Bellini College REU Symposium. This USF-hosted event
offers a distinctive opportunity for the Bellini College community to explore new
undergraduate research pathways and for faculty to showcase upcoming research initiatives.
The symposium affirms the university's commitment to research excellence and
student achievement. </p>
<h3><strong>Hosted By: Alfredo Weitzenfeld, Phd</strong></h3>
<p>Director, REU Program<br />Email: <a href="mailto:aweitzenfeld@usf.edu">aweitzenfeld@usf.edu</a> </p>
<h3><strong>May 1, 2026</strong></h3>
<p>10:00 a.m. – 1:00 p.m.<br />Research Park – Seminar Room (First Floor)<br />3814 Spectrum Blvd., Tampa, FL 33620</p>
<table class="button-link-row-snippet" style="width: 100%;">
<thead>
<tr>
<th class="ou-help mceNonEditable">Button(s) - Centered<br /><em>To add more buttons to this set, insert a row for each button in the table below.</em></th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><a href="https://usf.az1.qualtrics.com/jfe/form/SV_bPBNpmRuB51qdPE">Register Now</a></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><br />The Symposium is a free event open to all USF students and faculty. Register by April
27, 2026 </p>
<h3>Lunch Provided</h3>
<p>Boxed lunches will be provided for the first 50 registrants and participating REU
students will be provided for those who register by April 27. Vegetarian meals will
be available. </p>
<h3>Event Schedule </h3>
<p>10:00 a.m. – 11:00 a.m. | REU program overview and student panel<br />11:00 a.m. – 12:00 p.m. | Faculty presentations of research labs<br />12:00 p.m. – 1:00 p.m. | REU student poster presentations</p>
<table class="button-link-row-snippet" style="width: 100%;">
<thead>
<tr>
