<h3>About the Symposium</h3>
<p>The Bellini College Research Experience for Undergraduates Symposium showcases the
innovative, faculty-mentored research conducted by undergraduate students in the Bellini
College of Artificial Intelligence, Cybersecurity and Computing.<br />This event highlights the impact of hands-on research experiences that prepare students
for graduate study, industry innovation, and advanced research careers.<br />The symposium provides a forum for undergraduate scholars to present their work, share
discoveries, and engage with faculty, peers, and industry partners.</p>
<h3>About the REU Program</h3>
<p>The Research Experiences for Undergraduates (REU) Program offers students the opportunity
to work closely with faculty on cutting-edge research projects across AI, cybersecurity,
and computing disciplines.</p>
<ul>
<li>Through immersive research engagement, students:</li>
<li>Gain real-world research experience</li>
<li>Develop technical and analytical skills</li>
<li>Build strong faculty mentorship relationships</li>
<li>Prepare competitive graduate school applications</li>
<li>Receive stipends and research support opportunities</li>
</ul>
<p>The program is designed to inspire and equip undergraduate students to pursue advanced
study and research-focused careers.</p>
<p>Acknowledgements: this is a collaboration between:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://testsite.usf.edu/ai-cybersecurity-computing/research/reu-program.aspx">Bellini College (REU Program)</a></li>
<li><a href="https://testsite.usf.edu/research-innovation/undergraduate-research/seri.aspx">OneUSF SERI</a></li>
</ul>
<table class="media-medium-right">
<thead>
<tr>
<th class="ou-help mceNonEditable">Image - Medium - Right <br />Image Dimensions - Width: 320 px, Height: 213 px* <br />* Recommended Height.</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class="image"><img src="{{f:79777685}}" alt="A speaker gestures animatedly while presenting to an audience of engaged participants seated in a well-lit room, with large windows showing greenery outside and a presentation displayed on a screen behind. The diverse group, including individuals in professional attire, appears attentive and interested in the topic being discussed." width="653" height="436" /></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>Symposium Highlights</h3>
<p>The REU Symposium offers:</p>
<ul>
<li>Formal undergraduate research presentations</li>
<li>Faculty research opportunity briefings</li>
<li>Information on advanced research training pathways</li>
<li>Insight into stipends, funding mechanisms, and academic advancement</li>
<li>Opportunities for scholarly networking and collaboration</li>
</ul>
<p>This event provides a meaningful venue for interdisciplinary dialogue and research
engagement within the Bellini College community and beyond.</p>
<h3>Funding Sponsors</h3>
<p>This program is supported by:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="/research-innovation/innovation-enterprise/florida-high-tech-corridor/undergraduate-research-initiative.aspx">Florida High Tech Corridor</a></li>
<li><a href="/research-innovation/research-support/funding-resources/researchone.aspx">ResearchOne</a></li>
<li><a href="https://cra.org/ur2phd/">CRA UR2PhD</a></li>
</ul>
<p><em>For reasonable accommodations, please contact us at <a href="mailto:Bellini-CollegeEvents@usf.edu">Bellini-CollegeEvents@usf.edu</a> </em></p><!-- /com.omniupdate.div -->
